# Page Object Model

All UI interactions and locators belong in page objects. Specs orchestrate flows and assert outcomes only.

## Layout

- Page objects: `pages/**/*.ts` (e.g. `pages/HomePage.ts`)
- Specs: `tests/**/*.spec.ts`
- Shared flows: `pages` methods or fixtures — not duplicated locator chains in specs

## Rules

- Specs must not call `page.getBy*` / `page.locator` for product UI — use page object methods.
- Each page object takes `page: Page` in the constructor and exposes intent-named methods (`login`, `openCart`).
- Locators are private fields or private getters on the page object.
- Do not put assertions inside page objects unless the method’s job is an expect helper; prefer asserting in the spec.

## Example

```typescript
// pages/LoginPage.ts
import { type Page, type Locator } from '@playwright/test';

export class LoginPage {
  private readonly email: Locator;
  private readonly password: Locator;
  private readonly submit: Locator;

  constructor(private readonly page: Page) {
    this.email = page.getByLabel('Email');
    this.password = page.getByLabel('Password');
    this.submit = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign in' });
  }

  async goto() {
    await this.page.goto('/login');
  }

  async login(email: string, password: string) {
    await this.email.fill(email);
    await this.password.fill(password);
    await this.submit.click();
  }
}
```

```typescript
// tests/login.spec.ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
import { LoginPage } from '../pages/LoginPage';
import { DashboardPage } from '../pages/DashboardPage';

test('user can sign in', async ({ page }) => {
  const loginPage = new LoginPage(page);
  const dashboard = new DashboardPage(page);
  await loginPage.goto();
  await loginPage.login('user@example.com', 'secret');
  await expect(dashboard.heading).toBeVisible();
});
```

Expose assertion targets as `readonly` locators on the page object (e.g. `readonly heading: Locator`) when the spec needs `expect(...)`. Never inline product UI locators in the spec.
